  "description": "ImgSmush is a pure-C# image codec with no native dependencies. It quantizes 32-bit RGBA into high-quality 8-bit palette (indexed) PNGs - median cut, k-means refinement, edge-aware Floyd-Steinberg dithering - and encodes WebP: lossy (VP8) with a lossless alpha channel, and lossless (VP8L). It also reads PNG and still WebP (lossy + lossless) back to RGBA, verified bit-exact against the libwebp reference. MIT licensed, zero-dependency, AOT-friendly.",
